{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "66be8ce4-06e9-4e2a-a588-1a5cc228b8e7",
    "name": "Legault GW Customer API — Direct (dev)",
    "description": "Direct, service-level contract for the customer API — what the **auth layer** sends, not what the mobile app sends.\n\nUse this collection when you are working on this service itself: it sets `x-brand` and `x-customer-id` by hand, so it bypasses the auth layer entirely. In every deployed environment the service must be reachable **only** through the auth layer; these headers are injected there and any client-supplied copy is stripped.\n\nThe mobile-facing contract lives in `postman/` one level up (`Legault Customer API — Mobile`).\n\nRouting\n- `/health` and `/health/ready` are unversioned and brand-agnostic (liveness / readiness probes).\n- Everything else is mounted under `/{version}` (currently only `v1`) and requires the `x-brand` header (`rens` or `mondou`).\n- Member endpoints additionally require `x-customer-id` and an `Authorization: Bearer <SLAS access token>` header.\n\nAddress ids in the path are the **local** uuid returned as `id` by the API (not the SFCC `addressId`). `Create Address` stores it in the `addressId` environment variable automatically.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "apiVersion",
      "value": "v1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Fallback used when the environment does not define apiVersion."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Probes and brand configuration echo.",
      "item": [
